{"event_type":"review","id":"8686136efaf1b9d67efbd14ceee2f9a54d541405e45ecee5dbcdd7be564146cf","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T19:50:33Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c59090b0318090da3eb1849345ffe01e93246a23c263f27fda56f4a5cacb673d","sha256":"c59090b0318090da3eb1849345ffe01e93246a23c263f27fda56f4a5cacb673d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cd0ef15e7f612cac3e16f1debf98cf9ce96672dacfec092bdfc32e9a956ca74d","sha256":"cd0ef15e7f612cac3e16f1debf98cf9ce96672dacfec092bdfc32e9a956ca74d"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3fbfd91a5238931da2adae4ac305843afbe0326f201a77ef4fa4c7b60b49c4d4","sha256":"3fbfd91a5238931da2adae4ac305843afbe0326f201a77ef4fa4c7b60b49c4d4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b38c3b2f385fbb5ce07a13f114d16cf8cb19f0f4584e612dbb41044a329c7a99","sha256":"b38c3b2f385fbb5ce07a13f114d16cf8cb19f0f4584e612dbb41044a329c7a99"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/898f3b6aaec295ac0101ce632b357b6326e00c5553d478867a81861acadfa788","sha256":"898f3b6aaec295ac0101ce632b357b6326e00c5553d478867a81861acadfa788"}],"attempt_id":"a9556abdd48bb7f1752551add4b4ce73e988a547ede88d905a56c4085d44264f:0:1","base":"2b45dcbfcc3bdd56e680bd2ac08754c1422b8bd3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"8ef491ff81610717562ba5fe13322689faba80b2","body":"**Restore the saved service using its own start timeout.**\n\n`restore_activation` starts the restored service with `_service_start_timeout(unit, inventory)` (unit-adapter.py:1846). That helper returns the pinned template's `TimeoutStartSec` plus `COMPLETION_MARGIN_SECONDS` (1257-1261). The restored file comes from the snapshot, not the pinned template. Nothing in this file reads that file's `TimeoutStartSec`. A saved `Type=oneshot` service can therefore declare a longer start bound than the pinned template. If its healthy start runs longer than the pinned bound plus margin, the `start` command hits its timeout and restoration refuses. For example, a saved service that allows 20 minutes, with a pinned template that allows 5 minutes, gives a 360-second command timeout.\n\nThe install path at line 1634 is correct, because it starts the newly rendered pinned unit. The defect is limited to the restore path.\n\nDerive the restore start timeout from the saved unit's `TimeoutStartSec`, using the same template-section parser. Alternatively, refuse restoration when the saved value differs from the pinned value.","id":"d17323d976b989582495e4c8e03f08e2ee61ed40635de451e196d376592f362d","intervals":[[1258,1258]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-adapter.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Restore the saved service using its own start timeout."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"8ef491ff81610717562ba5fe13322689faba80b2","body":"**Select the restore check from the saved service type.**\n\n`restore_activation` chooses its post-start check from the pinned template type, `inventory[unit][\"service_type\"]` (line 1861). It does not use the `Type=` directive of the service file it restores. Nothing on the path rejects a mismatch. A saved `Type=simple` unit with a pinned `oneshot` template can reach restore. If the restored simple service exits cleanly before `_show` runs, `ActiveState=inactive` passes the oneshot branch and restore reports success even though the snapshot recorded `service_active=active`.\n\nDerive the service type from the saved service bytes, and apply the check for that type. Refuse when the type is missing or unsupported.","id":"78251005d9c3618c5dd9e4918e427b8cc75b034f4b901f2cbdf3e05fac79865e","intervals":[[1861,1861]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-adapter.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Select the restore check from the saved service type."}],"head":"848bc639e0636ffe6b7b9d0ccac12d97dce32f1d","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"114b0109491136f965b9727d382dda13e662191a","intervals":[[1,386]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/UNIT-SWITCH-DESIGN.md"},{"blob":"7510442d31a1abe0246871aceed83d7d6708399d","intervals":[[1,382]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/VM-FEASIBILITY.md"},{"blob":"8ef491ff81610717562ba5fe13322689faba80b2","intervals":[[1,1938]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-adapter.py"}],"job_id":"a9556abdd48bb7f1752551add4b4ce73e988a547ede88d905a56c4085d44264f:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"114b0109491136f965b9727d382dda13e662191a","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/UNIT-SWITCH-DESIGN.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7510442d31a1abe0246871aceed83d7d6708399d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/VM-FEASIBILITY.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"8ef491ff81610717562ba5fe13322689faba80b2","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-adapter.py","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"114b0109491136f965b9727d382dda13e662191a","intervals":[[69,69]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/UNIT-SWITCH-DESIGN.md"},{"blob":"7510442d31a1abe0246871aceed83d7d6708399d","intervals":[[366,368],[370,370],[372,372]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/VM-FEASIBILITY.md"},{"blob":"8ef491ff81610717562ba5fe13322689faba80b2","intervals":[[1526,1526]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-adapter.py"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"114b0109491136f965b9727d382dda13e662191a","intervals":[[69,69]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/UNIT-SWITCH-DESIGN.md"}